+/* PATCHED (semantius-app): the `no-scrollbar` utility is removed.
+
+   Upstream ships it on CommandList, SidebarContent and Combobox, which hides the
+   scrollbar on a list that still scrolls and puts no other cue in its place — the
+   list just looks like it ends. See shadcn-ui/ui#9527 and the two PRs that would
+   remove it upstream (#9534, #9611), both open and unmerged.
+
+   It has to be deleted HERE rather than overridden from our own CSS. An override
+   can undo `scrollbar-width: none`, but cancelling
+   `::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none }` means writing our own rule for that
+   pseudo-element — and in Blink and WebKit the mere PRESENCE of an author rule on
+   `::-webkit-scrollbar` switches the element from overlay scrollbars to custom
+   ones. That is a different non-default, not the OS default. Redefining the
+   `@utility` does not work either: Tailwind MERGES a second definition into the
+   same rule instead of replacing it (measured, not assumed).
+
+   Dropping the `@import "shadcn/tailwind.css"` line would remove the class too,
+   but that file also carries nine `@custom-variant` definitions (data-open,
+   data-closed, data-checked, data-unchecked, data-selected, data-disabled,
+   data-active, data-horizontal, data-vertical) used ~99 times across src/, and
+   data-checked's selector is not equivalent to Tailwind's built-in. The import
+   stays; only this one utility goes.
+
+   Guarded by apps/web/src/test/shadcnNoScrollbar.test.ts, which compiles the real
+   CSS and fails if the rule reappears. If shadcn merges the upstream fix this
+   patch stops applying, loudly, and can be deleted. */
 
